The _Swift_ BAT spectrum is \\nu F_{\\nu}\\propto\\nu^{0.5\\pm 0.4} in the 15-350 keV range (Barthelmy et al. 2005), implying E_{\\rm p}\\gtrsim 300 keV, which is hard to achieve for internal shocks (see Eq. 4). Possible ways of increasing E_{\\rm p} are if (i) the internal shocks are highly relativistic, rather than mildly relativistic as assumed above, or (ii) only a small fraction of the electrons are accelerated to relativistic energies (e.g. Ramirez-Ruiz & Lloyd-Ronning 2002). It is not clear how likely either of these options is. The constraints on the physical parameters in the internal shocks model are summarized in Fig. 2.

